            "text": "An efficient implementation that resolves the timeout by leveraging multi-threaded BLAS matrix multiplication (`GEMM`) in 64-bit precision to compute all pairwise squared Euclidean distances simultaneously via $\\|x_i - x_j\\|^2 = \\|x_i\\|^2 + \\|x_j\\|^2 - 2\\langle x_i, x_j \\rangle$.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the vectors and promote to float64 for full numerical precision\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n\n    # Compute squared L2 norms for each row\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X * X, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix using high-performance GEMM: G = X @ X.T\n    G = X @ X.T\n\n    # Form squared distance matrix in-place: D^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2 * (x_i . x_j)\n    G *= -2.0\n    G += sq_norms[:, None]\n    G += sq_norms[None, :]\n\n    # Zero the diagonal exactly\n    np.fill_diagonal(G, 0.0)\n\n    # Clamp any small negative values due to floating-point roundoff to 0\n    np.maximum(G, 0.0, out=G)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distance matrix in-place\n    np.sqrt(G, out=G)\n\n    total = float(G.sum())\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
